---
/**
 * /ai-news — "AI Signal": the autonomous daily AI-news desk. Every story is
 * researched, written, gated, and published end-to-end by the /ai-news
 * pipeline (.claude/skills/ai-news/SKILL.md) — the disclaimer IS the
 * marketing: this page is a live demo of an autonomous pipeline in
 * production. Rolling window (standard 14d / major 21d, see
 * src/data/news.ts) — an instrument, not an archive. No per-story pages;
 * cards link out to their sources.
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import MarketingLayout from '../../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import NewsStory from '../../components/NewsStory.astro';
import DeskSchematic from '../../components/DeskSchematic.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import { formatEntryDate } from '../../data/dates';
import { visibleFilter, sortByPublished, currentSpotlight, newsSchema } from '../../data/news';

const entries = (await getCollection('news', visibleFilter)).sort(sortByPublished);
const spotlight = currentSpotlight(entries);
const stream = spotlight ? entries.filter((e) => e.id !== spotlight.id) : entries;
const origin = new URL(Astro.site!).origin;
const storyCount = String(entries.length).padStart(2, '0');
// Build timestamp — daily pipeline pushes mean this refreshes daily; if runs
// stop, this readout self-discloses the staleness.
const builtAt = new Date();
// Desk facts — build-time, honest by construction: the newest visible story's
// own date, and the day the desk went autonomous (first live sweep).
const DESK_SINCE = new Date('2026-07-06T12:00:00-04:00');
const lastStory = entries[0]?.data.publishedAt;
---
<MarketingLayout
  title="AI News"
  description="The AI developments that matter, summarized with implications — researched, written, and published daily by an autonomous AI pipeline. Every story links to its sources."
  image="/og/ai-news.png"
  schema={newsSchema(origin)}
  rssHref="/ai-news/rss.xml"
>
  {/* ── Intro ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      D113 CARRIED OFF THE HOME PAGE, 2026-09-13. This page ran four bands at
      max-w-4xl, 3xl, 3xl and 4xl — two widths an inch apart — on one ground,
      with one rhythm, and the spotlight and the stream separated by nothing at
      all: the spotlight carried no bottom padding, so the strongest story of
      the window and the list it leads flowed together as one column of cards.

      It now walks feature, popout, popout, content for the column and canvas,
      canvas, canvas, deep for the ground, with the rhythm running regular,
      tight, regular, tight under both and a hairline closing the spotlight. The
      palette does none of the work — a hue is the lightest signal on a page,
      which is the argument src/components/kit/industrial.js makes under WHY
      THREE AND NOT SEVEN.

      ── NO STORY CARD GETS A PAINTED GROUND, AND THAT IS A MEASUREMENT ───────

      The stream was built onto `deep` first and verify-bands.mjs failed it: the
      "Major" tier chip measured 3.71:1 against a 4.5 floor. Chasing that turned
      up something older and worse. NewsStory.astro sets that chip as an inline
      literal, `color: var(--color-warn)`, and warn is #9a6b06 — which ON THIS
      PAGE AS IT SHIPS TODAY, on plain canvas, measures 4.39:1. It is under the
      floor already and has been, live, with nothing able to see it:
      check-contrast.mjs reads token pairs somebody declared and an inline style
      on a component declares no pair, and this page carried no row in
      verify-bands.mjs at all. Every ground available here makes it worse —
      surface composites to about 4.1 and deep to 3.71 — so the reshape does not
      get to spend one on the cards. The chip is a palette question and the
      palette is locked, so it is reported rather than changed.

      THE SPOTLIGHT BAND COULD NOT HAVE CARRIED ONE EITHER, for a second and
      independent reason. It renders only when the desk has flagged a story
      `spotlight` — data/news.ts returns null otherwise — so a ground here would
      be a band that exists on some days and not others, and the row measuring it
      would red the build on a day the desk simply flagged nothing. That is a
      content decision reported as a defect.

      SO THE ONE GROUND GOES TO THE CLOSING ASK, the only band on this page whose
      every word was written here rather than overnight. It always renders, it
      carries no chip, and it is what verify-bands.mjs measures.

      THE WEAKEST SEAM IS SPOTLIGHT TO STREAM, named rather than glossed. Both
      are the same component at the same measure and the ground is spent, so the
      separation is the rhythm plus a rule — two of the five heavy signals
      industrial.js names, and both of them more than the nothing that was there.

      NOTHING MOVED AND NOTHING WAS CUT. The readout line, the desk schematic
      and the fragment-jump script at the foot all sit where they were written,
      and the script's two measured reasons for existing are untouched.
      Reshaping is not reordering. */}
  <Section width="feature" class="border-b border-line">
    <Fragment slot="backdrop">
      <div class="bg-grid bg-grid-fade pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 -z-10 opacity-60"></div>
    </Fragment>
      <p class="mono-label">AI Signal — autonomous news desk</p>
      <h1 class="statement mt-3 max-w-3xl">
        The signal, not the noise.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        The AI developments that actually matter — summarized, with what they mean for operators,
        businesses, and people. Stories rotate on a two-to-three-week window; the strongest story
        holds the spotlight.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Full disclosure, as a feature:</span> every story on
        this page was researched, written, fact-gated, and published end-to-end by an AI pipeline
        I built — no human in the loop. Every story links to its sources.
        <span class="text-ink">This page is the product demo.</span>
      </p>
      {/* Readout line */}
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 font-mono text-xs tracking-wide text-ink-faint">
        <span class="mono-label inline-flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="status-dot"></span>
          Autonomous
        </span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>Stories: {storyCount}</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>Window: 14–21 days</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>Desk running since: {formatEntryDate(DESK_SINCE).split(' · ')[0]}</span>
        {lastStory && (
          <>
            <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
            <span>Last story: {formatEntryDate(lastStory).split(' · ')[0]}</span>
          </>
        )}
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <span>Updated: {formatEntryDate(builtAt)}</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        <a href="/ai-news/rss.xml" class="link-sweep">Feed: RSS →</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
        {/* Blog de-listed 2026-08-24 — see SiteHeader for the reason. */}
      </div>

      {/* The Desk Readout — the pipeline itself, as an instrument panel */}
      <div class="mt-8">
        <DeskSchematic />
      </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── Spotlight ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The reading column and the shortest rhythm, against the widest band on
      the page. No ground, and the header above gives two separate reasons.

      IT NOW HAS A BOTTOM EDGE, which is the part a reader will actually feel
      and the rule that does half the work of separating this band from the
      list under it. It carried `pt-16 sm:pt-20` and no bottom padding at all,
      so the one story the page calls strongest ran straight into the rest with
      nothing between them — not a gap, not a line, nothing. */}
  {spotlight && (
    <Section width="popout" density="tight" class="border-b border-line">
      <p class="mono-label inline-flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="status-dot"></span>
        Spotlight
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4">
        <NewsStory entry={spotlight} featured />
      </div>
    </Section>
  )}

  {/* ── The stream ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      The standard rhythm returns, at the spotlight's measure deliberately: the
      card above and every card here are the same component rendering the same
      shape of story, and moving the column between them would say they are
      different kinds of thing. The rule at the foot of the band above says
      what is true instead — one of them was picked out, and these are the rest.

      THE GROUND THAT BELONGS HERE IS THE ONE THIS PAGE CANNOT SPEND. A list
      this long is what a heavier ground is for, and `deep` was measured on it
      before it was given up: the "Major" chip came back at 3.71:1. The header
      above carries the whole reading, including the 4.39:1 the same chip
      measures on the canvas it is standing on right now. */}
  <Section width="popout">
    {/* `space-y-5` MOVED OFF THE SECTION AND ONTO THE STACK ITSELF, and it had
        to. It used to sit beside `mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16` on the
        <section>, where the cards were its direct children. Section.astro puts
        a centering div between the two, so a class passed through `class`
        lands on the section and spaces that ONE div against nothing — the
        cards would have closed up against each other with no error anywhere.
        One wrapper, one existing utility, no new class. */}
    <div class="space-y-5">
      {stream.map((entry) => <NewsStory entry={entry} />)}
      {entries.length === 0 && (
        <div class="panel p-8 text-center">
          <p class="mono-label">No stories in the current window</p>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-md leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            The desk publishes only when something clears the bar — zero is a valid day. Check back
            tomorrow.
          </p>
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* ── CTA — the page is the demo ─────────────────────────────────────────
      THE PAGE'S ONLY PAINTED GROUND, out to a wider column, at the shortest
      rhythm — three signals against the stream above, and the only band here
      every word of which was written in this repo rather than overnight. It
      carries no chip, it renders on every build, and it is the row
      scripts/verify-bands.mjs stands on for this page.

      The column opening back up is what tells a reader the list has ended. The
      old band carried `pb-20` and no top padding at all, so it read as the tail
      of the last story card rather than as the page's own ask. */}
  <Section tone="deep" width="content" density="tight" class="text-center">
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-3xl">
      This page is the demo.
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      An autonomous pipeline researched, wrote, gated, and shipped everything above — daily,
      unattended. Want one running on your problem?
    </p>
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3">
      <Button href="/contact/" variant="primary">Start a project</Button>
      <Button href="/work/" variant="secondary">See the live tools</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/* Deep-link support for /ai-news/#<story-id> — the links /ai-news/rss.xml
      hands to feed readers. TWO things break a plain fragment navigation here,
      and neither shows up in the markup or throws anything:

        1. Every story is a `.reveal` target, so it sits at opacity 0 until
           BaseLayout's IntersectionObserver catches it. A browser will scroll
           to a fully transparent element quite happily and the reader still
           sees a blank screen — so scrolling alone is not enough.
        2. The native fragment scroll does not survive this page's boot.
           MEASURED on production 2026-07-28: loading /ai-news/#<valid-id> left
           scrollY at 0 with the target 1,948px down the page.

      So reveal the target explicitly, then scroll it ourselves. `scrollIntoView`
      honors the card's `scroll-mt-20`, which is what clears the sticky header.
      Guarded so a bad or stale fragment (stories expire) is simply ignored and
      the visitor lands on the page as normal. */}
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var jump = function () {
        try {
          var id = decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1));
          if (!id) return;
          var el = document.getElementById(id);
          if (!el) return;
          el.classList.add('is-visible');
          el.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'instant', block: 'start' });
        } catch (e) {}
      };
      if (location.hash) {
        if (document.readyState === 'complete') jump();
        else window.addEventListener('load', jump);
      }
      window.addEventListener('hashchange', jump);
    })();
  </script>
</MarketingLayout>
